Hermes patch: an unqualified computer_use capture skips desktop panels and docks.
Base: ~/taffy/hermes at 74943bb889 (Oct 9, 2026). Apply: cd ~/taffy/hermes && git apply ~/taffy/patches/hermes-computer-use-skip-panels.patch

Why (docs/qa/2026-10-09-school-browser.md): on the Bot Desktop (Xfce) the window manager stacks the two
xfce4-panel windows above every normal window, and cua-driver reports that stacking as z_index. capture()
with no app took the frontmost window, the 88x44 launcher dock at the bottom of the screen, so School's
capture came back "88x44 app=Xfce4-panel, 0 interactable elements" while Chromium was open behind it.
The fix adds panel and dock app names to the existing "not a real app window" filter that implicit Linux
captures already apply. Asking for the panel by name (app="Xfce4-panel") still captures it.
Tests: tests/tools/test_computer_use_capture_panel_window.py (fails before, passes after); all
tests/tools/test_computer_use*.py pass (251 passed, 8 skipped).

